			"year": 1450,
			"yearLabel": "c. 1450",
			"title": "The Kisra kingdoms",
			"text": "Borgu tradition says Kisra, a rival of the Prophet driven from Arabia, led his people to the Niger; his sons founded Bussa (Woru), Nikki (Shabi) and Illo (Bio), parting at Gunji. Before them Borgu's villages lived by lineage and rarely fought. Historians read the legend as the memory of mounted invaders of the 15th century, whose descendants, the Wasangari, ruled as a warrior class bound by mutual defence.",
